# --- T113-driven firmware patch path (field-flash the supervisor) ---
# The T113/USART link above lands on the STM32 PA2/PA3 = USART2, which
# IS the STM32G0 ROM system-bootloader UART. So the host reflashes the
# supervisor in-field two ways, no ST-Link, box stays sealed:
#   1) normal: the running app takes a new image over UART and self-
#      flashes (or software-jumps to system memory), then reboots;
#   2) recovery: even if the app is bricked, the T113 drives BOOT0 high
#      and pulses NRST -> STM32 lands in the ROM bootloader on USART2
#      and the host reflashes it with the stock ST protocol.
# J10 (SWD) stays for factory bring-up / setting nBOOT_SEL=0.
boot0_ctl = Net('MCU_BOOT0_CTL')
tc('PD16', mcu_nrst)      # T113 -> STM32 NRST (open-drain reset/recover)
tc('PD15', boot0_ctl)     # T113 -> BOOT0 select (high = ROM bootloader)
